-- title:
--   Ω_{F/K} is free of rank one over a separable extension of K(x)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and let $x \in F$ be an element transcendental over $K$, i.e. not algebraic over $K$. Assume that $F$ is a separable algebraic extension of the intermediate field $K(x) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {x}` generated by $x$ (the hypothesis `Algebra.IsSeparable (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F`, which includes that every element of $F$ is algebraic over $K(x)$ with separable minimal polynomial). The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions about the module $\Omega_{F/K}$ of Kähler differentials of $F$ over $K$, regarded as an $F$-module: it is a free $F$-module, and its rank `Module.finrank F Ω[F⁄K]` equals $1$. No finiteness hypothesis on the extension $F/K(x)$ is imposed, and no basis is exhibited in the statement itself (the assertion is freeness together with the numerical value of the rank).
--
--   This is the standard computation that a function field in one variable which is separably generated has a one-dimensional space of Kähler differentials, $\Omega_{F/K} = F\,dx$. It feeds the construction of curves over a field in this development, being cited by [`AlgebraicCurve.isCurveOver_of_transcendental`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.isCurveOver_of_transcendental) and by [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_isCurveOver_adjoin_range_eq_top_apply_algEquiv_eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_isCurveOver_adjoin_range_eq_top_apply_algEquiv_eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_kaehlerRankOne_of_transcendental.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open KaehlerDifferential

theorem AlgebraicCurve.kaehlerRankOne_of_transcendental
    {K F : Type*} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F]
    {x : F} (htr : Transcendental K x)
    (hsep : Algebra.IsSeparable (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F) :
    Module.Free F Ω[F⁄K] ∧ Module.finrank F Ω[F⁄K] = 1 := by sorry
